```bash
# Development build (larger binary, includes debug symbols)
wasm-pack build --target web

# Release build (optimised; wasm-opt runs automatically if installed)
wasm-pack build --target web --release
```

The `--target web` flag tells `wasm-pack` to produce an ES module that can be imported directly in a browser without a bundler. Alternatives include `--target bundler` (for webpack/rollup/vite) and `--target nodejs`.

The output in `pkg/` will contain, among other files:

- `<crate_name>_bg.wasm` — the compiled wasm binary.
- `<crate_name>.js` — the JS glue module, including the `init()` function.
- `<crate_name>.d.ts` — TypeScript declarations.

